1
00:00:16,480 --> 00:01:50,350
 Stars, galaxies, in astral seas above, on cosmic paths we'll trace, man's over wings, the T is such a wondrous thing, behind us all come see, come take your place, we're leaving soon for-

2
00:01:50,350 --> 00:02:05,350
 At least the last one in this little ship, what a shame.

3
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:13,800
 You know, Metro, these days if you find a quiet corner of space you should be glad there are not many of them, but what you say is true, it really is for the last time.

4
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,780
 Sad to think that it's ending.

5
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:18,800
 Our Pierrot is going to be commanding a cruiser.

6
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:21,860
 And our Mercedes is going to be his second officer.

7
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:24,670
 She'll accept the offer I made her and we'll all stay together.

8
00:02:25,130 --> 00:02:28,140
 Yes, and I'll be made third mechanic, chief cook and bottle washer.

9
00:02:28,260 --> 00:02:30,460
 My duties will be checking circuits, as usual.

10
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:33,260
 What a waste of talent. No telling how far I'd go if I had the chance.

11
00:02:33,770 --> 00:02:35,050
 Metro, you're talking nonsense.

12
00:02:35,370 --> 00:02:37,410
 You know very well you'll go on as a full partner.

13
00:02:37,890 --> 00:02:41,450
 Hey, what do you say a little spin through Nebula NGC 6188, huh?

14
00:02:41,570 --> 00:02:45,090
 There's open-faced mining going on and a couple of pretty interesting planets.

15
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:47,590
 Well, what do you say, Lieutenant?

16
00:02:47,910 --> 00:02:51,050
 Oh, I think you'd better ask our distinguished scholar and bottle washer.

17
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:53,790
 What do you say, Metro? Are we going to find life in a nebula?

18
00:02:54,390 --> 00:02:58,860
 Why not? That one there has a cloud of space dust that absorbs stellar radiation.

19
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:03,240
 With no trace of any toxic gases, a conducive environment for life, so as I say, why not?

20
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:08,280
 But I'd be a little bit careful if I were you. The region is infested with asteroids of irregular trajectories.

21
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:11,690
 Well, Lieutenant, what are you waiting for? Program us for the flight.

22
00:03:12,070 --> 00:03:12,570
 Aye, aye, Captain.

23
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:48,030
 Assure you, they possess prodigious power.

24
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:49,920
 Oh, yes, prodigious.

25
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:56,390
 Power, or should I say their power to execute orders, for they can really execute those orders, right?

26
00:03:56,550 --> 00:03:58,590
 I give the orders and they execute them real good.

27
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:01,510
 You could say I am the head and they are the arms.

28
00:04:01,650 --> 00:04:03,150
 You get it? I give the orders.

29
00:04:05,230 --> 00:04:11,270
 All those guys on Omega will have to watch it because we're getting ready for a real, genuine, authentic stroke of genius.

30
00:04:11,550 --> 00:04:11,950
 Tell them.

31
00:04:12,010 --> 00:04:14,560
 Yeah, what he says, a regular stroke of genius.

32
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:21,590
 But General, it's just that, aren't you afraid with all that force, that power which our science puts into their hands,

33
00:04:21,830 --> 00:04:24,990
 that one day these allies might decide to turn against us as enemies.

34
00:04:25,420 --> 00:04:27,460
 Bunch of nonsense, all that you said.

35
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:29,240
 You forget, I'm a smart fellow.

36
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:30,440
 They produce for us.

37
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:31,320
 Yes, that's true.

38
00:04:31,710 --> 00:04:33,720
 But they're only like a lot of tools.

39
00:04:33,980 --> 00:04:36,320
 We've taken intelligent precautions, believe me.

40
00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:38,500
 The secrets of how it all works,

41
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:41,040
 the engines and spaceships, the computers, the brains,

42
00:04:41,140 --> 00:04:42,080
 that's yours truly.

43
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:43,970
 I mean, it is us, we alone.

44
00:04:44,530 --> 00:04:46,850
 Your words be heard on high in the cosmos,

45
00:04:46,850 --> 00:04:48,950
 because if they ever did turn against us,

46
00:04:49,170 --> 00:04:51,830
 there is no telling how much destruction they could unleash.

47
00:04:52,990 --> 00:04:56,260
 Enough of this pussyfooting around, okay?

48
00:04:56,260 --> 00:04:58,970
 As soon as we're ready, the universe is ours!

49
00:04:58,970 --> 00:05:00,370
 Who is this ally?

50
00:05:00,370 --> 00:05:02,870
 Where are you now?

51
00:05:02,870 --> 00:05:06,250
 Soon all is going to be revealed, you'll know in good time.

52
00:05:06,250 --> 00:05:23,680
 Patience, don't worry, you'll know that in good time.

53
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:34,810
 ...are ready and in position for carrying out phase two of Exercise D.Va, Great Computer.

54
00:05:34,810 --> 00:05:40,640
 Order operation to begin launch and carry out mission as planned.

55
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:45,360
 Yes, Great Computer, at your orders.

56
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:49,710
 The star is at least four times larger than our sun.

57
00:05:49,710 --> 00:05:52,800
 Fortunately, we're shielded from its rays by space dust.

58
00:05:53,540 --> 00:05:57,080
 These planets appear to be located at distances favorable to the creation of life.

59
00:05:57,920 --> 00:06:00,480
 Optimum distance is 200 times the star's diameter.

60
00:06:05,130 --> 00:06:11,090
 Think we should fire on them without warning?

61
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:21,580
 It isn't us they're after, but let's try to get out of their way.

62
00:06:34,410 --> 00:06:48,290
 It's really incredible.

63
00:06:49,010 --> 00:06:49,410
 Incredible.

64
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:51,320
 We'll have to call Omega.

65
00:06:51,970 --> 00:06:52,890
 No, Pierrot.

66
00:06:53,090 --> 00:06:54,940
 I don't think that they know we're here.

67
00:06:54,940 --> 00:07:00,200
 As far as they're concerned, we're just another bit of asteroid out in space that's gravitated here.

68
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:03,180
 If we send a message, they'll find us, and we'll be vaporized.

69
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:04,240
 Let's find out more.

70
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:05,850
 Yes, you're right, Psyche.

71
00:07:24,310 --> 00:07:30,090
 History of the exercise.

72
00:07:30,870 --> 00:07:31,740
 Ready, Admiral.

73
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:49,180
 Success for the exercise, Admiral.

74
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:50,580
 Return to base.

75
00:07:53,010 --> 00:07:54,400
 Astonishing.

76
00:07:55,030 --> 00:07:55,510
 Unbelievable.

77
00:07:56,020 --> 00:07:58,500
 It is indeed, I must admit, rather surprising.

78
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:00,100
 Careful now.

79
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:01,220
 They're turning around.

80
00:08:17,860 --> 00:08:35,100
 It is astounding.

81
00:08:35,260 --> 00:08:38,480
 Every arm of that monster must weigh 100,000 tons.

82
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:39,920
 Altogether, astounding.

83
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:44,260
 Yes, that's why they assemble it out in space where it's a weightless condition.

84
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:45,540
 They come from each planet.

85
00:08:45,890 --> 00:08:48,800
 All history, we have never known anything so powerful.

86
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:51,900
 We'll follow them, but now we have to notify Omega.

87
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:54,710
 Okay, Captain, I'm calling now.

88
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:09,140
 Urgent message for Colonel Pierre. Let me speak to him.

89
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:34,680
 Transmit that information to Cassiopeia.

90
00:09:36,170 --> 00:09:36,650
 Distraction.

91
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:39,060
 Give the General a chance to feel important.

92
00:09:40,370 --> 00:09:42,610
 At your orders, great computer, sending signal.

93
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,300
 Suggested General.

94
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:48,620
 That lousy hummingbird again, those busybodies from Omega.

95
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:50,480
 I don't believe it. It's always them.

96
00:09:50,620 --> 00:09:53,220
 Whatever I do, they're always right there snooping around.

97
00:09:56,650 --> 00:10:01,050
 Can see things. We'll get her. We'll get her.

98
00:10:01,050 --> 00:10:03,430
 Capture her and then get her to tell us her secrets.

99
00:10:03,670 --> 00:10:04,690
 How she doesn't, yeah.

100
00:10:05,230 --> 00:10:07,520
 With her mental powers, we'll be invulnerable.

101
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:11,010
 General, in our last encounter with her, we learned nothing.

102
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,140
 She learned all.

103
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:14,280
 You let her get away, you clumsy idiots.

104
00:10:14,580 --> 00:10:16,600
 Only this time, you gotta hold on to her.

105
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:19,640
 That nuisance with her, I don't care what you do with them.

106
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:20,720
 Just get them out of the way.

107
00:10:21,110 --> 00:10:23,920
 But that psyche, don't let her get away.

108
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:25,060
 She's got special powers.

109
00:10:25,650 --> 00:10:27,470
 And that's not all she's got, Chief.

110
00:10:27,890 --> 00:10:30,680
 See you around, Chief.

111
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:58,800
 I'm certain these are the same ones that we saw back when we were on Saturn.

112
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:00,040
 Humanoids?

113
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:02,600
 Can't shoot our way out. There are too many of them.

114
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:04,530
 Don't do what they say. We'll have to trick them.

115
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:09,390
 If we can make it as far as that spacecraft before they fire on us, we can use it for cover.

116
00:11:09,530 --> 00:11:10,030
 Let's try.

117
00:11:10,750 --> 00:11:13,180
 I think we're inventing a new sport.

118
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:15,400
 It's like being a clay pigeon in a shooting gallery.

119
00:11:18,900 --> 00:11:38,020
 Fire back. What do you think?

120
00:11:38,190 --> 00:11:40,750
 In my view, they're not firing to shoot us down.

121
00:11:40,750 --> 00:11:44,450
 They're only trying to impress us. Otherwise, we would already be space dust.

122
00:11:47,250 --> 00:11:53,810
 Remember Jurgle's lesson?

123
00:11:54,430 --> 00:11:56,670
 Well, now we can check on whether you're right, Metro.

124
00:11:57,130 --> 00:11:58,150
 If not, so long.

125
00:12:16,010 --> 00:12:28,410
 Starting engines.

126
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:52,100
 Stabilizers.

127
00:12:52,550 --> 00:12:59,130
 All damage. Emergency landing gear. Now it's our only hope.

128
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:07,060
 Well strapped in, Metro? I'm really sorry, only we haven't enough landing equipment. We only have two, not three.

129
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:11,520
 I know, I know. I assure you I am much more shock resistant than you think, my friends.

130
00:13:12,020 --> 00:13:15,210
 Now you go on. Don't waste any time. And I'll be seeing you.

131
00:13:47,940 --> 00:15:45,050
 We're there. We'll live. Came down near here.

132
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:48,550
 Lizard men. Regions infested with them.

133
00:15:48,730 --> 00:15:53,850
 One we seek has fallen into their clutches very long since ceased to be a problem.

134
00:15:53,850 --> 00:16:05,310
 It looks as if they've left. We must remain watchful all the same. They will return.

135
00:16:05,450 --> 00:16:06,490
 He is still delirious.

136
00:16:11,230 --> 00:16:13,680
 And this one had to fight the Lizardmen for,

137
00:16:13,880 --> 00:16:16,580
 and whom we must keep hidden from those up in the castle

138
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:18,500
 who will soon scrutinize our region.

139
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:20,840
 What misfortune is yet to befall him?

140
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:23,900
 We are human, Robert, and we care about him.

141
00:16:24,200 --> 00:16:25,780
 All right, Sylvia, we'll take care of him.

142
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:26,810
 You take care of him.

143
00:16:31,110 --> 00:16:35,190
 Medical services must make her strong enough

144
00:16:35,190 --> 00:16:36,730
 to voyage from Epis to Yama.

145
00:16:37,410 --> 00:16:38,520
 Pan in the captain.

146
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:41,440
 No sign of individual, great computer.

147
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:42,980
 We are continuing the search.

148
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:44,020
 Have alerted all units.

149
00:16:44,950 --> 00:16:46,070
 This is annoying.

150
00:16:46,270 --> 00:16:48,480
 He must be found and liquidated.

151
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:51,500
 Otherwise, the entire D.Va plan may be compromised.

152
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:57,260
 Use every available need to locate him or his remains, Class A priority.

153
00:16:57,870 --> 00:17:00,900
 Order understood. It will be done, Great Computer.

154
00:17:09,180 --> 00:17:18,660
 Ah, you are awake. You gave us a great deal of worry. Now we are relieved.

155
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:22,160
 All of us now want to welcome you to our planet Apis.

156
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:32,760
 Well, this is as far as we go. Now we go back.

157
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:36,380
 Why should we go back now? It's very nice around here. Let's look around.

158
00:17:36,990 --> 00:17:40,930
 No, Piero, we can't. There are creatures here that are terribly dangerous.

159
00:17:41,370 --> 00:17:44,670
 And don't forget all of those up in the castle that are looking for you. They're worse.

160
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:48,580
 But then why do you stay here, Sylvia? It sounds like an awful place.

161
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:52,400
 That's just it. Nobody would ever think of looking for us here.

162
00:17:53,410 --> 00:17:57,460
 You see, we are outlaws, rebels. There's just a handful of us.

163
00:17:57,890 --> 00:18:02,680
 My brother Giglio is a leader. He's the only person I have in this whole world, and I have...

164
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:03,400
 Watch it, Sylvia!

165
00:18:07,550 --> 00:18:22,450
 Hero?

166
00:18:23,120 --> 00:18:24,890
 Quickly, to the cave.

167
00:18:34,750 --> 00:18:45,140
 Little farther.

168
00:18:52,160 --> 00:19:01,360
 This is going to be a very short trip, you will see.

169
00:19:01,630 --> 00:19:02,740
 Where are you taking me?

170
00:19:03,150 --> 00:19:03,910
 To Yama.

171
00:19:04,190 --> 00:19:06,230
 The neighboring planet, our big sister.

172
00:19:06,670 --> 00:19:08,410
 It is she who directs the whole system.

173
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:11,000
 All living conditions are better there.

174
00:19:11,430 --> 00:19:13,870
 And you will be very well cared for.

175
00:19:14,130 --> 00:19:15,850
 Everything is there to treat your illness.

176
00:19:16,730 --> 00:19:20,200
 We are only a lookout post here, only a few of us.

177
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:23,140
 The real fight is on Yama, the neighboring planet.

178
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:26,090
 That is where the castle is, the enemy headquarters.

179
00:19:26,410 --> 00:19:28,010
 Here, life is too harsh, too hard.

180
00:19:28,010 --> 00:19:33,260
 For example, even the Cassiopeans who came to settle here couldn't bear it and left.

181
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:34,740
 That will give you an idea.

182
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:36,460
 A new race took their place.

183
00:19:37,150 --> 00:19:38,290
 They built another base.

184
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:41,800
 They were insensitive to the climate and wild animals,

185
00:19:42,270 --> 00:19:44,410
 to everything that makes human life difficult.

186
00:19:44,710 --> 00:19:44,930
 Why?

187
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:47,510
 Because they are robots, no more, no less.

188
00:19:47,790 --> 00:19:50,690
 They are making terrible weapons of destruction, experimenting.

189
00:19:51,070 --> 00:19:52,150
 But you had a demonstration.

190
00:19:52,310 --> 00:19:54,810
 Chief, they have taken the young lady over to Yama.

191
00:19:55,350 --> 00:19:58,820
 Your young friend left the planet this morning aboard a spaceship.

192
00:19:59,250 --> 00:20:01,750
 A frigate of the official fleet took her to Yama.

193
00:20:01,750 --> 00:20:04,120
 Where can I get a ship so that I can go there?

194
00:20:05,810 --> 00:20:08,050
 You want to get a spaceship?

195
00:20:08,350 --> 00:20:11,610
 You must be dreaming, my land. A spacecraft from Apis? Oh, no.

196
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:17,650
 It's of utmost importance, I assure you, and it seems to me we're fighting on the same side as I see it.

197
00:20:17,650 --> 00:20:18,400
 You have to help me.

198
00:20:18,940 --> 00:20:20,260
 Better you should wait here.

199
00:20:20,690 --> 00:20:21,750
 There are two advantages.

200
00:20:22,030 --> 00:20:25,220
 One, they think you're dead, and the castle people won't look for you.

201
00:20:25,470 --> 00:20:27,200
 Two, you should get your strength back.

202
00:20:27,590 --> 00:20:29,950
 No, there isn't any time to lose.

203
00:20:30,210 --> 00:20:34,300
 Listen to me. We have no spacecraft, and I don't know where you'll get one.

204
00:20:34,300 --> 00:20:36,060
 Unless Murdoch would do it.

205
00:20:36,750 --> 00:20:38,390
 There is no guarantee that he'd agree.

206
00:20:39,140 --> 00:20:41,480
 He's a smuggler and a sort of bandit, I guess.

207
00:20:41,730 --> 00:20:43,760
 But he's a thousand kilometers from here.

208
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:45,560
 Will you take me to him?

209
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:48,340
 A thousand kilometers across this wretched land,

210
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:51,660
 infested with creatures more ferocious than those in any nightmare,

211
00:20:51,780 --> 00:20:53,980
 with every enemy patrol out looking for you.

212
00:20:54,230 --> 00:20:55,580
 No thanks, I'd rather not.

213
00:20:56,300 --> 00:20:57,840
 Omega will reward you.

214
00:20:58,070 --> 00:20:58,990
 Listen to me, Captain.

215
00:20:59,470 --> 00:21:01,090
 Rewards are of no interest to us.

216
00:21:01,430 --> 00:21:04,860
 No reward you could name is worth facing what is certain death.

217
00:21:05,560 --> 00:21:07,910
 All right, show me the direction I'll go alone.

218
00:21:07,910 --> 00:21:09,410
 You'd be a fool to go alone.

219
00:21:09,590 --> 00:21:11,090
 You know nothing of this planet.

220
00:21:11,650 --> 00:21:13,350
 And you, Robert, you don't know me.

221
00:21:13,650 --> 00:21:17,120
 I've been in tighter situations than this, and I've found a way out of them.

222
00:21:17,530 --> 00:21:18,740
 I will go with them.

223
00:21:18,940 --> 00:21:21,520
 If I have to die, I'd rather go down fighting. I'll go.

224
00:21:21,770 --> 00:21:23,170
 I'll go with you, too, Piero.

225
00:21:24,510 --> 00:21:27,290
 Good care of those weapons.

226
00:21:27,690 --> 00:21:29,750
 There are most precious possessions here.

227
00:21:34,660 --> 00:21:39,080
 Giglio, you look worried.

228
00:21:39,660 --> 00:21:43,500
 Piero, you have been warned there can be ugly surprises around any corner.

229
00:21:43,580 --> 00:21:45,540
 With every step, we're walking into danger.

230
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:47,000
 Stay alert if you want to stay alive.

231
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:48,050
 Oh, what a climate.

232
00:21:48,250 --> 00:21:50,870
 What place? What sort of creatures are we going to find?

233
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:52,090
 You'll see.

234
00:21:52,430 --> 00:21:54,360
 But in any case, they'll mean trouble.

235
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:55,420
 That I guarantee.

236
00:21:55,660 --> 00:21:57,800
 The first ones we'll encounter are the Qubies.

237
00:21:58,130 --> 00:22:00,260
 With any luck, they'll let us have a mount.

238
00:22:00,930 --> 00:22:04,230
 If they don't give us one, it's unlikely that we'll ever make it alive.

239
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:08,020
 Well, if it's really as bad as you say, as dangerous, why did you agree to go with me?

240
00:22:08,180 --> 00:22:09,840
 It's not for you. I want that understood.

241
00:22:10,020 --> 00:22:11,960
 It's for my sister. She's all that I have.

242
00:22:14,390 --> 00:22:21,610
 These Qubies, at least, they're friendly, I hope.

243
00:22:21,830 --> 00:22:23,630
 I thought I'd already explained that.

244
00:22:23,730 --> 00:22:25,730
 Nobody is friendly anywhere on this planet.

245
00:22:25,730 --> 00:22:29,940
 The Qubies are, if you like, a little less ferocious than the others, but that's all.

246
00:22:30,260 --> 00:22:46,190
 Stay here till nightfall, because in the light, their gun sights couldn't miss us.

247
00:22:46,210 --> 00:22:49,690
 We may as well eat something. We'll need all our strength.

248
00:22:50,110 --> 00:22:50,700
 Piero.

249
00:22:57,850 --> 00:23:05,770
 Edge of the QBs.

250
00:23:08,290 --> 00:23:09,680
 Watch out!

251
00:23:12,420 --> 00:23:15,050
 Run, it's not healthy around here.

252
00:23:19,650 --> 00:23:27,930
 Friends, don't shoot us. Take us to your leader.

253
00:23:44,900 --> 00:23:53,050
 As to give them a weapon.

254
00:23:53,650 --> 00:23:54,210
 We do.

255
00:23:54,770 --> 00:23:56,150
 I still have my pistol.

256
00:23:59,290 --> 00:24:02,090
 Only keep an eye on them once they got it.

257
00:24:08,100 --> 00:24:23,450
 I think we should have waited till dawn.

258
00:24:23,870 --> 00:24:27,240
 Piero, we left where they realized that three weapons are better than one,

259
00:24:27,520 --> 00:24:30,000
 and that it wouldn't be difficult to get all three.

260
00:24:31,710 --> 00:24:35,300
 Giglio, let's head for the hummingbird.

261
00:24:35,480 --> 00:24:37,520
 It must have come down somewhere around here.

262
00:24:37,830 --> 00:24:39,540
 No, lose too much time.

263
00:24:39,540 --> 00:24:41,670
 Take unnecessary risks.

264
00:24:41,670 --> 00:24:43,950
 But we'll go there anyway. I insist. Let's go.

265
00:24:43,950 --> 00:25:06,710
 I'm beginning to wonder if they'd show up around here.

266
00:25:06,710 --> 00:25:10,030
 That is anyone civilized, not one of those ghastly robots again.

267
00:25:10,030 --> 00:25:12,660
 Metro! Knew I'd find you!

268
00:25:12,660 --> 00:25:20,320
 Tell me, how are you, Metro?

269
00:25:20,320 --> 00:25:23,570
 That pile of debris isn't gonna make things any easier.

270
00:25:23,570 --> 00:25:28,890
 This pile of debris has already performed heroic services, even saved our lives.

271
00:25:28,890 --> 00:25:31,130
 You'll see what I mean very soon.

